RF.put("questb:b29",{"8669":{"id":8669,"t":"Genesis Shoulderpads","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Strife Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nGenesis Shoulderpads\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Druid Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8669\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Genesis Shoulderpads this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8509":{"id":8509,"t":"The Alliance Needs Arthas' Tears!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 34.","obj":"Bring 20 Arthas' Tears to Sergeant Major Germaine at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Arthas' Tears Arthas' Tears in Razorfen Downs , Arthas' Tears , Spirit of Trey Lightforge 33.3 % , Treant Spirit 3.9 % and 4 more","desc":"I'll keep it simple and to the point, ‹class›. The Alliance needs to collect a large quantity of Arthas' Tears for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort. Don't ask me what for; I'm just following orders. But I'd like you to gather up as many of the herbs as you can and bring them back to me here. Are you willing to do that?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"What's that? Speak up, ‹class›! Have you got that shipment of Arthas' Tears I asked for?","done":"Good work, ‹class›. I must say that I'm pleasantly surprised. You would not believe the number of people that have come by, offering to help, but never returning. Let me just get those into a crate and tallied with your name on it, and then we can talk again about whether I need anymore of those plants.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.6,"n":"Sergeant Major Germaine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8589":{"id":8589,"t":"The Horde Needs More Heavy Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Heavy Leather to Skinner Jamani at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n10 Heavy Leather Advanced Target Dummy 90 % , Felsteel Chest 3.6 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 2.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 2.5 % and 4 more","desc":"It's true, ‹class›, I still need more heavy leather. The requests from the generals and their quartermasters seem endless. And that's nothing compared to what the zeppelin masters are asking for!\nI need to get my quota collected on the double. Baekun, bring me more stacks of heavy leather as soon as you can!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"You da mon, mon! Thank you so much for the heavy leather. Every little bit gets us that much closer. I'll just get these onto a pile so that the other leatherworkers can get to work on them.\nThanks again, ‹name›, and if you come across more stacks of heavy leather, you know where you can find me.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":73.3,"n":"Skinner Jamani","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"669":{"id":669,"t":"Sunken Treasure","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sample Elven Gem to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay.\nSample Elven Gem\nProvided: Sample Elven Gem","desc":"Fleet Master Seahorn will want to hear about our find at once.\nBut as you can see, we're not in much of a position to get out of here. Not only is the tide too low, but those damned creatures we disrupted are keeping a close eye on our movements.\nYou can be of great service to the Blackwater Raiders if you can get word to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay that we discovered the treasure and are working on extracting more. Take him this sample as proof.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"What brings you to Booty Bay, ‹class›?","done":"Ah, leave it to good old Shakes O'Breen! I knew that he was the right Captain for the mission!\nArathi Highlands Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":32.3,"y":81.4,"n":"Shakes O'Breen","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":77,"n":"Fleet Master Seahorn","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"909":{"id":909,"t":"Baron aquanis","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Strange Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\nProvided: Strange Water Globe","desc":"The defeated water elemental has left behind a strange water globe. You surmise that the object somehow fed the beast energy. Inside the globe, a putrid-looking form of water sloshes about. The globe itself seems impervious to any sort of physical force.\nIf anyone can make any sense of this item, it would be Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring. He is located at the Horde's Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOutlaw Sabre Witch's Finger\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\nLevel 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Horde Type Elite Quest ID 909","cats":["ashenvale"]},"8989":{"id":8989,"t":"The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth the spirit of Mor Grayhoof and slay him. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the recombined Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLord Valthalak's Amulet\nBrazier of Beckoning\nMor Grayhoof slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"My friend, Mor Grayhoof, was the first to fall victim to possession of a piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet, and the corrupting spirit fragment that it contains. After stealing Valthalak's spellbook and amulet, we fled for our lives from the upper portion of Blackrock Spire. Along the way, Mor fell into the lower portion of the spire.\nLater, we discovered that he survived the fall, only to be captured and tortured by War Master Voone. A few spectral assassins snuck in and slew him right in front of Voone.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Then it is done? You have retrieved the right piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet, recombined the amulet into one whole, and finally put to rest the spirit of my old companion, Mor Grayhoof?","done":"Thank you for helping Mor Grayhoof, ‹name›. Another spirit rests in peace, and we now have the reassembled amulet! But we still have the hardest test ahead of us.\nIn order for the brazier to be attuned to calling forth Lord Valthalak, there are a few more items that need to be gathered and brought back to me here.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"97949":{"id":97949,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Radnaal Maneweaver on the road to Darnassus from Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":42,"y":50,"n":"Radnaal Maneweaver","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94349":{"id":94349,"t":"Craftsmans writ heavy scorpid helm","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Heavy Scorpid Helm\nHeavy Scorpid Helm","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Heavy Scorpid Helm, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Scorpid Helm Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94349","cats":["crafting"]},"94269":{"id":94269,"t":"Craftsmans writ inlaid mithril cylinder","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Inlaid Mithril Cylinder\nInlaid Mithril Cylinder","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Inlaid Mithril Cylinder, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Inlaid Mithril Cylinder Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94269","cats":["crafting"]},"29":{"id":29,"t":"Trial of the Lake","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a Shrine Bauble in Lake Elune'ara, and take it to the Shrine of Remulos in northwestern Moonglade. Once there, use the Shrine Bauble.\nYou must speak with Tajarri at the shrine afterwards in order to complete the trial.","desc":"For your first trial, search the depths of Lake Elune'ara to locate a Shrine Bauble. It decays rapidly, so proceed with it to the Shrine of Remulos post haste. Use the bauble at the shrine, and then speak with Tajarri there; she is one of Moonglade's most trusted wardens.\nYou only have a set amount of time to complete the task, and you may be competing against other druids searching for baubles themselves. Mental and physical dexterity will be critical to your success.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Well now. It looks like yet another ‹race› has successfully completed the Trial of the Lake! Well done, my young friend - well done.\nAs I've said, my name is Tajarri. It is my duty and my privilege to serve as a warden for Moonglade, and specifically this shrine. Keeper Remulos guides the Cenarion Circle in preservation of nature and balance, and his shrine serves as a lasting tribute to such. By using the bauble here, it serves as a nod to the importance of this place within the Circle.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.5,"y":40.1,"n":"Tajarri","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"829":{"id":829,"t":"Neeru Fireblade","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Example Collar to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.\nExample Collar\nProvided: Example Collar","desc":"The Searing Collars you brought me are powerful, demonic implements. Divining their origin is, I'm afraid, beyond my skills as a shaman. We will need a warlock to study them.\nTake a searing collar to Neeru Fireblade. Although he is a skilled warlock, he professes to use his powers to thwart demons, and claims his research in the occult is benign. Be that true or false, we may need his aid against the demonic cult in Durotar.\nYou may find Neeru in Orgrimmar in the Cleft of Shadow.","rew":"Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"My most humble greetings, ‹class›. How might I help my ‹race› brother today?","done":"Ah, and where did you get this? Good Margoz in Razor Hill sent you to me, did he?\nWell, let me take a closer look...\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.4,"y":20,"n":"Margoz","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"269":{"id":269,"t":"Seeking Wisdom","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Jitters' Completed Journal to Bishop Farthing in Stormwind.\nJitters' Completed Journal\nProvided: Jitters' Completed Journal","desc":"Go to the city of Stormwind and speak with Bishop Farthing in the Cathedral of Light. Give him Jitters' journal and tell him you mean to face Morbent Fel.\nAlthough Stormwind has forsaken Darkshire, Farthing is a kind soul and very wise. He may help you on your quest to save us.\nYour mission is perilous, but hurry, ‹name›. With each passing hour, the shadows of Duskwood grow ever darker.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Rest, brother/sister. I can tell you have traveled far, and you bear a heavy burden. Can you tell me what casts that dark shadow over you?","done":"<After reading the journal and hearing your intent...>\nAn evil taint has gained a foothold within the already beleaguered Duskwood. I thank the Light we have a hero such as you to face it.\nBut you must first prepare yourself for the coming trial...for the Necromancer Morbent Fel is immensely powerful, and has cast dark enchantments about himself to protect him from physical assaults. If you are to defeat him, you will need a weapon that is proof against these protections.\nDuskwood Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.9,"y":46,"n":"Bishop Farthing","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"5149":{"id":5149,"t":"Pamela's Doll","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Pamela's doll.\nPamela's Doll","desc":"My auntie Marlene told me to stay here in our house because my father had to go and fight. My father's the bravest man in the whole world!\nBut I've been here for a long time, and he hasn't come for me. Sometimes bad people come and whisper to me and I want my dad to make them go away, but he's not here!\nAnd sometimes when it gets dark I want to play with my doll but I can't because I left it in town.\nWill you find my doll for me?","rew":"Experience: 2,800","back":"Did you find my doll?","done":"You found it! You found my doll! Oh, thank you!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"109":{"id":109,"t":"Report to Gryan Stoutmantle","lv":10,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Gryan Stoutmantle. He usually can be found in the stone tower on Sentinel Hill, just off the road, in the middle of Westfall.","desc":"Looks to me you've seen quite a bit of combat in your time, ‹class›. If you haven't already, you should report to Gryan Stoutmantle. He heads up the People's Militia, aimed at protecting the farmlands of Westfall. I bet he could use your help. You can usually find him in the stone tower on Sentinel Hill, just off the road in the middle of Westfall.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Ah, so my friend sent you here? How kind.\nWell the Stormwind Monarchy has abandoned our cause. Now it is up to the People's Militia to keep the land free from corruption. If our cause interests you, I can put your combat skills to use in the name of freedom.\nWestfall Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56,"y":31.2,"n":"Farmer Saldean","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":60,"y":19.4,"n":"Farmer Furlbrow","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24.2,"y":74.4,"n":"Deputy Rainer","s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3629":{"id":3629,"t":"Goblin Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Goblin Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Expert engineering yields two distinct disciplines: gnome and goblin. I only bother to mention goblin engineering because I'm a fair trainer. They like to make things that blow up, and they rarely care what is in the way - even themselves.\n‹name›, read this manual. If you want to learn how to blow yourself up, then take it to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure this is what you want before finishing his task.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"I can smell fresh recruits much like I can an excellent blasting powder - from a mile away. Have you come seeking to learn about the mastery of the explosion?","done":"Well ‹name›, you were wise to seek my tutelage! Any schlep can become an expert at the basics of engineering - the gnomes and their irradiated home of Gnomeregan are proof of that. It takes a strong mind and a steady hand (emphasis on STEADY) though to master the discipline of Goblin Engineering.\nKeep your ears perked ‹name›, and you might learn something.\nDun Morogh Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.1,"y":28.1,"n":"Springspindle Fizzlegear","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4109":{"id":4109,"t":"Salve via Mining","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Tainted Vitriol Gold Vein 50 % , Ooze Covered Gold Vein 50 % , Gold Vein 50 % , Mithril Deposit 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve","back":"If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.\nIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here's some Cenarion plant salve. If you find more vitriol when you mine in Felwood, remember to hold on to it for me! The more of it you find, the more salve I will be able to make.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"509":{"id":509,"t":"Elixir of Agony","lv":28,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Mudsnout Blossoms to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\n6 Mudsnout Blossoms Mudsnout Blossom","desc":"Another day, another elixir to be made. If it were up to me, I'd just let the pathetic humans and Scourge fight it out. They seem bent on killing each other as is.\nAlas, our Dark Lady wants to help speed up the process a tad so why not pass these morbid days by spreading a little death and disease across the land?\nHere's the plan, ‹name›: you go out to Nethander Stead, south of Tarren Mill and east of the river and Southshore. Collect for me 6 Mudsnout Blossoms from the field for my next elixir.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Swiftness Potion 5 Healing Potion\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Any luck at Nethander Stead?","done":"Ah, the horrible reek of Mudsnout Blossoms. At least those filthy Gnolls are good for something.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8909":{"id":8909,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with 1 set of Devout Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nDevout Bracers Crimson Priest 3.7 % , Crimson Initiate 1.9 % , Thuzadin Necromancer 1.6 % in Stratholme , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 1.3 % in Stratholme and 1 more","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"1949":{"id":1949,"t":"Hidden Secrets","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Magus Tirth in the Shimmering Flats.","desc":"To make your wand, there are key passages in a certain book that I must read. The book is called Rituals of Power, written by the Magus Tirth.\nI do not have a copy of his book, and none of the world's great libraries possess it. So you must speak with Tirth and gain it from him.\nGood luck. Tirth used to be a great mage and scholar, but now he spends his time at the gnome and goblin races in the Shimmering Flats, drinking and gambling.","rew":"Experience: 1,450","done":"What? Speak up! These old ears aren't as sharp as they used to be.\nWell, I hope you're here with a fresh mug of ale or some hot tips on the next race! If not, then you best keep walking... because I have a polymorph wand with your name on it!\nDustwallow Marsh Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.3,"y":75.7,"n":"Magus Tirth","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9389":{"id":9389,"t":"Flickering Flames in the Eastern Kingdoms","lv":25,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,500 experience instead of 15,000, 0.1 times as much.","obj":"Visit the bonfires within Hillsbrad Foothills, Silverpine Forest, Westfall, and the Wetlands, then speak with the Festival Flamekeeper.\nFlame of Hillsbrad used\nFlame of Silverpine used\nFlame of Westfall used\nFlame of the Wetlands used","desc":"The Midsummer Fire Festival traditionally lights up the land with a myriad of flames. Some argue that the green fires are the finest, as they are the hardest to maintain and have such a distinctive hue.\nMake sure they still burn in the Eastern Kingdoms for our Flamekeeper. They sit near Dun Modr in the Wetlands, close to Pyrewood Village within Silverpine Forest, on the cliffs overlooking the lighthouse in Westfall, and by the ruined tower in Hillsbrad Foothills.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Elderberry Pie 4 Fire-toasted Bun 5 Midsummer Sausage 5 Toasted Smorc\nExperience: 1,500","back":"Have you seen to your task?","done":"So you've returned, and you've seen to the emerald flames of the continent. What do you think, mm? A rare and wonderful sight, to be certain. I am aware, however, that tangible rewards are better appreciated... so please, take this for your trouble.\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City Thunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades Hillsbrad Foothills Silverpine Forest Westfall Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.6,"y":91.9,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.6,"y":34.2,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Festival Flamekeeper","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"749":{"id":749,"t":"The Ravaged Caravan","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Morin Cloudstalker wants you to examine the contents of a supply crate at the Ravaged Caravan.","desc":"A few days ago, we found a Venture Co. caravan traveling under guard on the northern shore of Stonebull Lake. We'd lost two of our number in an earlier battle, so we were quick to attack and lay waste to the caravan.\nWe left their supply crates, thinking that our torches would destroy anything of value, but given that Venture Co. salvagers have been spotted near the burned wagons, maybe we were wrong.\nPerhaps you could go to the caravan and examine the contents of the crates.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"All sides of the crate are stamped with the sign of the Venture Co. Mining Division. Notes printed carefully on the side of the carton indicate that the contents are due for processing at one of their central plants.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":54.8,"y":64.3,"n":"Morin Cloudstalker","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":51.9,"y":53.4,"n":"Sealed Supply Crate","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9069":{"id":9069,"t":"Earthshatter Legguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Earthshatter Legguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Legguards, 20 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 3 Arcanite Bars and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Legguards\n20 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Arcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Legguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Earthshatter Legguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9229":{"id":9229,"t":"The Fate of Ramaladni","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Naxxramas and uncover the Fate of Ramaladni.\nFate of Ramaladni Plague Slime in Naxxramas , Plague Slime (Blue) , Plague Slime (Red) , Plague Slime (Green) and 4 more","desc":"Ramaladni was a warrior of the Brotherhood - a pupil of Highlord Mograine before the Dawn even existed! When news of Mograine's death reached him, hatred and anger took over.\nUnderstand this, ‹name›, when rage and retribution take the reins, a man ceases to be a man. The man personifies the emotions that control him instead. And so it would be that Ramaladni, the spirit of retribution, would enter Naxxramas to exact vengeance... and never return.\nEnter Naxxramas and find what became of Ramaladni.","back":"Any news of Ramaladni?","done":"It is his ring! But it is destroyed. No other evidence of Ramaladni was found?\n<Korfax grimaces.>\nThis does not bode well for Ramaladni. The ring, however... it might be salvageable.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1789":{"id":1789,"t":"The Symbol of Life","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSymbol of Life","done":"Make haste, ‹name›, more than one life hangs in the balance if you fail.\nIf for some reason you fail to help Muiredon and Narm, then return to me and I will give you another Symbol of Life for your travels.\nDon't mistake my aid as simple charity, you must prove yourself worthy like any other ‹class› and continual failure may reflect upon you later.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5629":{"id":5629,"t":"Returning Home","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"Hello again, ‹name›. I know you've been busy aiding our people, but you must take some time for yourself also. Priestess Alathea sent someone here looking for you. It seems that you've caught the attention of our elders and they feel you are prepared for greater things. Head to the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus and look for Alathea there. She will be waiting. Good luck, and may Elune be with you.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards\nExperience: 210","done":"Wonderful, you've returned home, ‹name›. It always pleases Tyrande and myself when those we've trained go out into the world and return to us safely. How have things been with you? Does Elune still bless your travels? Perhaps after we speak more about the business at hand, you could tell me more of your travels.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.7,"n":"Laurna Morninglight","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8349":{"id":8349,"t":"Bor Wildmane","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.","desc":"Now that you have a medallion and can summon an Abyssal Duke, speak with Bor Wildmane. He will set you on a task against the Abyssal Council.\nGood luck, ‹name›. And if you ever need more medallions, return to me.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Good to see you again, ‹class›! So you had a medallion made? Good -- you'll need that for your next quest...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8829":{"id":8829,"t":"The Ultimate Deception","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Skin of Shadow, 3 Frayed Abomination Stitchings and 1 Twilight Cultist Robe to Aurel Goldleaf at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing XI in order to complete this quest.\nSkin of Shadow Skin of Shadow , Lady Illucia Barov 19 % in Scholomance , Risen Bonewarder 17 % in Scholomance , Risen Construct 17 % in Scholomance and 3 more\n3 Frayed Abomination Stitching Ramstein the Gorger , Venom Belcher 15 % in Stratholme , Bile Spewer 15 % in Stratholme , Patchwork Horror 15 % in Stratholme\nTwilight Cultist Robe Twilight Marauder 8 % , Twilight Marauder Morna 8 % , Twilight Overlord 8 % , Twilight Flamereaver 8 % and 4 more\nLogistics Task Briefing XI\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing XI","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer operates through innumerable layers of secrecy and deceit. While their actions are carried out in our world, they are planned in a place we have not yet been able to reach.\nWe've come to believe that the stones the Twilight's Hammer uses to summon their superiors allow for two-way transportation. To attempt to use them in this manner, we must replicate - to every last detail - a twilight emissary's robe.\nGather the necessary materials and bring them to Aurel Goldleaf, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nMark of Remulos\nExperience: 650\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"429":{"id":429,"t":"Wild Hearts","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. No longer rewards Minor Discolored Healing Potion, Recipe: Minor Discolored Healing Potion.","obj":"Gather 3 discolored worg hearts and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.\n3 Discolored Worg Heart","desc":"My brother Quinn was badly hurt by the ghoul, Ivar the Foul, and I don't know if he will heal properly without alchemical aid. Although I am not an apothecary, I do know that our apothecaries can make healing potions from the discolored hearts of worgs.\nGather such hearts and take them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher to the south. Then return here with the potion.\nYou can find plenty of worgs between here and Malden's Orchard to the east.","rew":"Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"My time is short, ‹class›, for the Dark Lady has charged me with a grave task.","done":"<Renferrel takes the hearts.>\nIt is troubling to hear our Deathstalkers have failed their mission.\nLet us hope that these failures are rare.\nI'll give you the potion in a moment, but here is its recipe - if those Deathstalkers find themselves in need of future aid, then perhaps you can give it yourself.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.5,"y":13.4,"n":"Rane Yorick","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"79949":{"id":79949,"t":"A web of lies debunking myths and legends","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"A Web of Lies: Debunking Myths and Legends","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nA Web of Lies: Debunking Myths and Legends (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"81949":{"id":81949,"t":"Legends of the tidesages","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Legends of the Tidesages","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nLegends of the Tidesages (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"3789":{"id":3789,"t":"Assisting Arch Druid Staghelm","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.","desc":"Excuse me ‹class›, but I'd like just a moment of your time if possible.\nThe Cenarion Circle in Darnassus is looking for seasoned adventurers such as yourself to lend them aid in a vital research project. While I do not know the specifics, I can inform you that none other than Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is spearheading this research.\nPlease - if you are interested, speak with him directly in the Cenarion Enclave within Darnassus proper.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Well now, ‹class›... since you were informed that I was leading this research myself, you obviously came as quickly as you could.\nNow that you are here, be sure to pay attention the first time I tell you the details; I have no desire to repeat myself.\nStormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":75.3,"n":"Innkeeper Allison","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"189":{"id":189,"t":"Bloodscalp Ears","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 15 Bloodscalp Ears and return them to Kebok in Booty Bay.\n15 Bloodscalp Ear Bloodscalp Scavenger 80 % , Bloodscalp Mystic 80 % , Bloodscalp Beastmaster 80 % , Bloodscalp Shaman 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Damn trolls! They've been killing off our agents in the jungle! I've already lost a good number of my best guards to skirmishes with them. The costs are piling up! How will I explain this to Baron Revilgaz?\nDecisive action... Think, Kebok... you weren't assigned to the post you have today for sitting around... I've got it! You... ‹name›, is it? You'll help me, won't you? There's money to be had!\nHere's the deal... you bring me the ears of fifteen Bloodscalp Trolls, and I'll compensate you well.","rew":"You will receive:\n8 Goblin Fishing Pole\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"You've had success I hope? All over the place, those trolls. Filthy devils.\nOh yes, that reminds me! Be sure to tell your friends, yes? We could use much assistance!","done":"Oh excellent, excellent. That'll help a little, for the present...\n<He trails off, grumbling about profit margins and costs...>\nWhat? You're still here? Reward? Oh, right... of course, here, take this... it should be more than enough.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27,"y":77.1,"n":"Kebok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"349":{"id":349,"t":"Stranglethorn Fever","lv":35,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 35 instead of 45.","obj":"Speak with Witch Doctor Unbagwa.\n10 Gorilla Fang Enraged Silverback Gorilla , Mistvale Gorilla 50 % , Jungle Thunderer 50 % , Elder Mistvale Gorilla 50 % and 4 more","desc":"Hi, ‹name›!\nSpeak with me friend Witch Doctor Unbagwa.","back":"Witch Doctor Unbagwa knows what Mokk the Savage like. Yes, yes!\nMe speak with spirits and make he come, I do.\nBut other Gorilla-beast like spirit talkin' too. You protect Witch Doctor Unbagwa and I make he come to you.\nWitch Doctor Unbagwa want something first. You bring a Gorilla Fang and me start spirit talking!","done":"Witch Doctor Unbagwa like Gorilla Fangs! For you I talk to spirits. Make Mokk the Savage come.\nYou protect Witch Doctor Unbagwa from other Gorilla-beast through or no Mokk for you!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.3,"y":60.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Unbagwa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"589":{"id":589,"t":"The Singing Crystals","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Pulsing Blue Shards to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\n3 Pulsing Blue Shard Ironjaw Basilisk 80 %","desc":"Legends tell of a jewel, hidden deep in the heart of Stranglethorn. We call it the Mind's Eye, and it has great powers. If you gain this Eye then, perhaps, we can use it to bring lost Yenniku back from the darkness.\nI will consult with the spirits of the jungle to find the Mind's Eye. While I do this, you enter the Crystalvein Mine, southeast of here, and gather Pulsing Blue Shards from Ironjaw Basilisks. The shards are rare, but we will need their magic to bend the Mind's Eye to our will.","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Do you have the shards, ‹name›? They are needed for my final ritual, after we have the Mind's Eye.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. These shards are well formed. Already I hear them sing to me.\nAnd while you were gone, I spoke with the spirits of the jungle. I know where the Mind's Eye rests...\n...And who guards it.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.3,"y":27.7,"n":"Kin'weelay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1389":{"id":1389,"t":"Draenethyst Crystals","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Draenethyst crystals to Magtoor at The Harborage in the Swamp of Sorrows.\n6 Draenethyst Crystal Draenethyst Crystals","desc":"The lost ones who live in the Fallow Sanctuary look as we look, but they are monsters... driven mad by the rigors of our journey to Azeroth. Once our brethren, they now live in the Fallow Sanctuary to the east, catching or killing any who wander near.\nAnd they have stolen something sacred to us--draenethyst crystals.\nWe lack the force to enter the Fallow Sanctuary and reclaim our stolen draenethyst from among their huts and campfires, but without those crystals... we too may lose our way.","rew":"Experience: 2,750","back":"Do you have the crystals?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. We, are in your debt.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":26,"y":31.4,"n":"Magtoor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"4509":{"id":4509,"t":"Calm Before the Storm","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Pestlezugg's Un'Goro Report to Zilzibin Drumlore in Orgrimmar.\nPestlezugg's Un'Goro Report\nProvided: Pestlezugg's Un'Goro Report","desc":"My recent findings and the knowledge we have gained here today needs to reach hands that can quite possibly do something with it. As resourceful as we are here in Gadgetzan, we can't do this alone.\nTake my latest report back to Zilzibin Drumlore in Orgrimmar; he's still in his place on the upper part of the Drag, is he not? He's got friends who are high within the Horde; if we can get them involved in this ‹name›, then we just might make it out of this alive.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"They are fools, ‹name›! They cannot even think to look around them for a greater threat; their irrational hatred of the Alliance will be our undoing. I do not know how much more proof I can give them of the silithid threat short of dropping them in one of the hives so they can see for themselves!\nI'm sorry, you bring news for my attention?","done":"While I genuinely appreciate this, I am not sure what good it will do us. The Horde ignores threats from any source other than the Alliance. While Thrall himself might take action were the facts presented to him, he is beset on all sides by conflicting advice. These fools would have us chase our own imaginary tails were they to think it might catch the Alliance unawares!\nYou have seen the threat yourself, ‹name›. We must remain committed to defeating the silithid!\nTanaris Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":56.3,"y":46.7,"n":"Zilzibin Drumlore","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2749":{"id":2749,"t":"An Ordinary Egg","lv":60,"min":42,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ordinary Egg","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Rations\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Ordinary hippogryph eggs hatch about half the time. We do our best to nurture them and with a little luck, they will hatch.","done":"So, you have found an ordinary egg, ‹name›? Please give it to me... And we can only hope for the best.\nI don't have much, but please accept this reward. If you ever find yourself in Feralas again, know that I am always here to take the eggs you find there.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8749":{"id":8749,"t":"The Path of the Protector","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You honor my kind, ‹name›. Strike down the enemies of Kalimdor! Show them what it means to deface the land of eternal starlight.\nYou have earned another enhancement. Hand me your signet ring so that I may bolster its power.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the protector!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"1069":{"id":1069,"t":"Deepmoss Spider Eggs","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Deepmoss Eggs to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\n15 Deepmoss Egg Deepmoss Eggs 80 %","desc":"Spider egg omelettes are a new fad in Booty Bay! The problem is... Booty Bay's got no eggs.\nI smell an opportunity!\nIn Windshear Crag and Sishir Canyon, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the northwest, lives the deepmoss spider. Bring me its eggs and I'll pay a bundle!\nIn Windshear Crag, the eggs will be clustered under what trees remain.\nIn Sishir Canyon... well, if you have a weak stomach then maybe you should just collect the eggs at Windshear Crag...","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Did you get the eggs, ‹name›? I already made a shipping deal with Wharfmaster Dizzywig!","done":"You got them! Thank you!\nI'll have these sent to Dizzywig and get them shipped to Booty Bay. I can already taste the profits!\nHere is your cut, ‹name›. I couldn't have made this deal without you.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":37.6,"n":"Mebok Mizzyrix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1469":{"id":1469,"t":"Rhapsody's Tale","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Atal'ai Tablet Fragment to Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind.\nAtal'ai Tablet Fragment\nProvided: Atal'ai Tablet Fragment","desc":"Before the flight, I drank me a whole keg of stout. Hiccup!\nAnd what a flight it was. Zipping around with Brohann following me. Didn't see no temple though. Hiccup!\nWell, didn't see no temple till I got a little too tipsy and fell off my mount. I plunged right into the water and was sucked down. Found myself surrounded by a bunch of creepy trolls. Sure swam out of there fast! Even made off with this troll souvenir. Here, take it to Brohann and let him know his temple is down there, indeed. Hiccup!","rew":"Experience: 2,700\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"At long last you have returned, ‹name›. It has been quite some time since we last spoke. I thought perhaps you had forgotten about my quest.\nDid you locate that wily gryphon rider? Did he have anything to report?","done":"Rhapsody Shindigger! That's right... how could I forget such a name?\nSo he knew about the sinking of the temple all along? Well, that certainly would have saved you some leg work.\nBut this Atal'ai artifact! Why, it's quite a find!\nThe Hinterlands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":26.9,"y":48.6,"n":"Rhapsody Shindigger","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.5,"y":40.4,"n":"Brohann Caskbelly","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"2989":{"id":2989,"t":"The Altar of Zul","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Check the top of the Altar of Zul, then return to Gryphon Master Talonaxe.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Sharpbeak was not with the Witherbark trolls. Perhaps the Vilebranch trolls took him. Go to the Altar of Zul on the western edge of Vilebranch territory and search for the gryphon child.","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"Hurry, ‹name›! If the Vilebranch trolls have Sharpbeak, then who knows what they might be doing with him!","done":"Sharpbeak wasn't there? That is bad news, but it is good news too...\nIt is good that he was not at the Altar of Zul for the Vilebranch trolls are known for performing sacrifices.\nI thank you for all of your aid, but I'm afraid I have an even greater task ahead.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1149":{"id":1149,"t":"Test of Faith","lv":26,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you have faith, leap from the planks overlooking Thousand Needles.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"So, you have sought me out, or perhaps destiny brings you to me? No matter. You are here now, and so your journey will begin anew.\nMany facets make up a being: the spirit, the body, the mind. Some of these can be measured by a culture's traditions. Others we can only hope exist within ourselves. If you agree, I shall test some of the facets within you.\nIf you pass, then you shall become stronger. If you fail, then you will realize the vastness of the Nether.\nThe first is a Test of Faith.","rew":"Experience: 1,050\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Faith. It is far more important than some realize.\nIt does not matter what you believe sometimes. It is just important that you believe in something.","done":"It is not until faced with unforeseen adversity that we begin to see how strong our spirits are. You took the leap of faith even though you had no guarantees that you would survive. Your mind is open, and your spirit is prepared for what is to come.\nIf you are willing, then the next of your tests is ready.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.9,"y":41.5,"n":"Dorn Plainstalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7629":{"id":7629,"t":"Imp Delivery","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Imp in a Jar to the alchemy lab in the Scholomance. After the parchment is created, return the jar to Gorzeeki Wildeyes.\nImp in a Jar\nParchment Created\nProvided: Imp in a Jar","desc":"There is one more process required for Mor'zul's parchment; I need paper infused with Xorothian stardust. And... I'm afraid I can't do that here. I don't have the equipment!\nThere is an alchemy lab, however, with everything needed. It's in the Scholomance, on the isle of Caer Darrow in the Plaguelands.\nI can't make the trip, but here - take this jar. There's an imp inside who is quite clever. Let him out at the alchemy lab and he'll infuse the parchment.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you been to the Scholomance, ‹name›? Has the imp yet infused the parchment with the stardust?","done":"Ah, good. J'eevee created the parchment. How was the Scholomance? Charming, don't you think? And the bugs there... I hear they're delicious!\nWell done, ‹name›, and thank you for returning my jar. I've had it for a long time... and it's not for sale!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1709":{"id":1709,"t":"Klockmort's Creation","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Hardened Gauntlets\nExperience: 3,050","done":"Here's your armor, ‹name›. Furen's process worked brilliantly! Perfectly! Marvelously, truly!\nYou could run this armor over with a siege engine and it would spring right back into shape!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62,"y":28.5,"n":"Klockmort Spannerspan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"7789":{"id":7789,"t":"Quell the Silverwing Usurpers","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Alliance, gain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and bring it to Captain Shatterskull at the Mor'shan Base Camp.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, ‹race›. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor. Return to me with such a mark, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The blood of our enemies is a mark of honor. Do you have such a mark?","done":"<Captain Shatterskull roars in triumph.>\nHow much more can they withstand? How many more Alliance filth must perish at the hands of the Horde for them to retreat? Only time will tell, ‹race›...\nLevel 25 , requires level 20 Difficulty 20 21 23 28 33 Side Orc, Undead, Tauren, Troll Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7789","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8429":{"id":8429,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5229":{"id":5229,"t":"Target: Felstone Field","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Felstone Field in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there. It may have a key that will allow access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Felstone Field Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nFelstone Field Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Bilemaw\nEmpty Felstone Field Bottle\nProvided: Empty Felstone Field Bottle","desc":"Of the four cauldrons in the Western Plaguelands, the one at Felstone Field may be the easiest one to gain access to. The Scourge have greener troops positioned here, though they should not be underestimated.\nGo to Felstone Field, due east of here and northwest of Andorhal, and engage the cauldron lord there. On it is a key that will unlock access to the cauldron. When unlocked, use this bottle to get a sample of the cauldron's toxins; we'll need it for study in developing a counter agent.","rew":"Experience: 5,250\n+100 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"The key taken from Cauldron Lord Bilemaw is a perfect fit in unlocking the access panel, though it disappears after you use it. Still, you think you can open the panel now without a key. A foul stench emanates from the opened panel as an unknown mix of concentrated substances swirl inside the cauldron.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":37.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92109":{"id":92109,"t":"My first alchemy set","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 5 Empty Vials, 5 Silverleaf, and 5 Peacebloom to the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.\n5 Empty Vial\n5 Peacebloom\n5 Silverleaf","desc":"Erm... 'Ello, <mister/miss>. I'm not supposed to talk to strangers, but... Hey, what are those shiny bottles sticking out of your backpack for? Are you an alchemist? That's so cool!\nWhen I grow up, I want to be an alchemist too. Daddy won't let me play with any of his herbs; too dangerous, he says.\nWell, I want to start learning now. Could you maybe get some supplies for me, pretty please?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Minor Healing Potion Scribbled I.O.U.\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420","back":"'Ello again! Did you bring back alchemy stuff?","done":"Oh my gosh! Look at these! Did you pick the herbs yourself?\nWow, thanks mister, I am going to see what I can make with these right now! Do you want to watch?\nStart Odd Child End Odd Child Level 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 92109\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 10, 840 XP in all.\n1 [ 10 ] My First Alchemy Set this quest\nGather 5 Empty Vials, 5 Silverleaf, and 5 Peacebloom to the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.\nOdd Child\n420 XP\n2 [ 10 ] My First Real Potion\nGather 3 Murloc Eyes for the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.\nOdd Child\n420 XP","cats":["westfall"]},"92909":{"id":92909,"t":"Harvesting the harvesters","lv":15,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm wants you to bring him 14 Golem Isosprings and 5 Harvester Gyrostabilizers.\n14 Golem Isospring\n5 Harvester Gyrostabilizer","desc":"Oh no... I'm in for it now!\nI heard about the harvesters terrorizing the fields of Westfall, so I traveled all the way from Ironforge to see if I could recalibrate them. But they're far more aggressive than my calculations anticipated, and they chased me into this stable!\nIf I had some isosprings and gyrostabilizers from the harvesters, I could build a device to cover my escape. Could you gather the parts for me?","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 800\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"It's a mess out there, Theto! Did you collect the parts I need?","done":"Thanks a bunch! I'll get to work on an escape plan. In the meantime, take this!\nWestfall Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":51.6,"y":32.2,"n":"Ozwin Ironsprocket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92749":{"id":92749,"t":"A dynamite plan","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Obtain 10 Coarse Dynamite from crafting, trading, or the auction house, then return to Sprite Jumpsprocket in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.\n10 Coarse Dynamite","desc":"Industrial sabotage? You've got my attention!\nWe'll start with some dynamite...","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Show me those explosives, Busch!","done":"This is a great start! Now to tie it all together... and add a little extra zing...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.6,"y":8,"n":"Sprite Jumpsprocket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98189":{"id":98189,"t":"Return the statuette","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Menethil Statuette to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep.\nProvided: Menethil Statuette","desc":"My goodness, it's--it's beautiful!\nThe Blind Princess was to deliver this to Menethil Harbor before tragedy struck. We were so close!\nI believe it was to be signed for by Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep just behind us. Why don't you do the honors of finishing the job?","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.4,"y":58.6,"n":"Karl Boran","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.8,"y":57.4,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"6029":{"id":6029,"t":"The Everlook Report","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Everlook Report to Argent Officer Garush at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nEverlook Report\nProvided: Everlook Report","desc":"I'm looking for a responsible individual to aid me in a small but nonetheless important matter. I'm here as a representative of the Argent Dawn's interests to the local governance of Everlook. I need to get a progress report to Argent Officer Garush at the Bulwark; it's a ways from here, located along the western fringe of the Western Plaguelands, east of Tirisfal Glades.\nIf I may be so bold - this would be a perfect means to introduce yourself to my superior and perhaps earn some work from him!","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+50 reputation with Everlook","back":"Greetings, ‹class›. On behalf of the Argent Dawn, I offer you safety and shelter while you are here at Bulwark. I might also offer you the chance to fight for a cause that's worth fighting for!","done":"Resourceful for a human, Gregor is. He's been dealing with the Steamwheedle Cartel for some time now, and has become an expert on the \"art\" of goblin negotiations. Though it's true that the goblins' primary loyalties lie with those who have the largest coin purses, they also know and respect the value of diplomacy. If anything, it provides them with repeat customers...\nAt any rate, the Argent Dawn acknowledges you for your effort. Please have this, with our thanks.\nWinterspring Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":39,"n":"Gregor Greystone","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.2,"y":68.4,"n":"Argent Officer Garush","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"93949":{"id":93949,"t":"Bugged","lv":8,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill Skyhoppers in Valanaar until you've eliminated 8 Enchanted Skyhoppers.\nEnchanted Skyhopper Exterminated : 0/ 8","desc":"We've been bugged.\nIt's skyhopper season in the lowlands, which means the pests are everywhere. One of the High Order mages reported that one of the insects that they killed had an enchantment of some kind placed upon it. When we inspected it closely it seems to be some sort of listening spell.\nWe suspect that the cult is using these enchanted insects as spies. Go and exterminate them for us. You won't be able to tell which are enchanted by looking at them, so you'll just have to kill them all.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700","done":"I'm sure there are more of these critters around Valanaar, but every enchanted skyhopper we stomp out makes the city just a tiny bit safer.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8109":{"id":8109,"t":"Kezan's Unstoppable Taint","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Kezan's Taint","rew":"You will receive:\nKezan's Unstoppable Taint\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Call forth your demons, ‹class›. Let them bask in the energy of Kezan's Taint. Command them on the field of battle! Decimate the enemy!\nYes... The time has come to apply the final enhancement to Kezan's Taint. Give me the talisman.","done":"Flay the flesh from their corpses. Watch as the shadows consume the Hakkari. Draw power from their fear, ‹class›. Let Kezan's Taint augment this power...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]},"8189":{"id":8189,"t":"Presence of Sight","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Voodoo Slave 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Cub 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Tiger 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nPresence of Sight\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8189","cats":["zulgurub"]}});